option.RT_MODE=Ray Tracing
value.RT_MODE.0=Off (shadow map)
value.RT_MODE.1=Auto
value.RT_MODE.2=Always
option.RT_MODE.comment=Auto uses your Mac's ray-tracing hardware when mcmetal is installed, and a shadow map otherwise.
screen.LIGHT=Lighting
screen.COLOUR=Colour
screen.WORLD=World
screen.SEASON_PAGE=Seasons
option.SUN_STRENGTH=Sunlight
option.SKY_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Sky Light
option.LABPBR=PBR Resource Packs
option.LABPBR.comment=Uses normal and specular maps from LabPBR resource packs: bumpy surfaces, shiny metal, glowing details.
option.RT_PBR_EMISSIVE=PBR Glow in Rays
option.RT_PBR_EMISSIVE.comment=Glowing details of LabPBR resource packs (lamps, ores, lava) also light up rooms and show in reflections.
option.TAA=Anti-Aliasing (TAA)
option.TAA.comment=Smooths jagged edges and shimmering plants by blending frames.
option.BLOOM=Bloom
option.BLOOM.comment=A soft glow around the sun, lights and other bright things.
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Bloom Strength
option.LENS_FLARE=Lens Flare
option.LENS_FLARE.comment=A camera's lens flare from the sun: soft coloured ghosts across the screen. Off by default.
option.DEPTH_OF_FIELD=Depth of Field
option.DEPTH_OF_FIELD.comment=Like a camera: things nearer or further than what you look at go soft. Off by default.
option.DOF_STRENGTH=Depth of Field Blur
option.DOF_STRENGTH.comment=How quickly things go soft away from the focus.
option.MOTION_BLUR=Motion Blur
option.MOTION_BLUR.comment=A soft blur while turning and moving, like a camera's shutter. Off by default.
option.MOTION_BLUR_STRENGTH=Motion Blur Amount
option.MOTION_BLUR_STRENGTH.comment=How long the camera's shutter stays open.
option.SHADOW_FILTER=Shadow Smoothing
option.SHADOW_FILTER.comment=Smooths the grain out of ray-traced sun shadows, keeping the edges between objects sharp.
option.LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH=Lens Flare Strength
option.CLOUDS=Soft Clouds
option.CLOUDS.comment=Our own soft cloud layer instead of Minecraft's blocky clouds.
option.CLOUD_AMOUNT=Cloud Amount
option.CLOUD_SPEED=Cloud Speed
option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS=Volumetric Clouds
option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS.comment=Clouds with real height: shaded by themselves, glowing at the edges towards the sun. Off: a flat layer (faster).
option.CLOUD_STEPS=Cloud Quality
option.CLOUD_STEPS.comment=Samples through the clouds per pixel. More is smoother but slower.
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud Shadows
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS.comment=The clouds' shadows drift over the land.
option.CLOUD_SHADOW_STRENGTH=Cloud Shadow Strength
profile.LOW=Low (M1, M2: aims for 60 fps)
profile.SMOOTH=Smooth (bounce light at a quarter rate: for 120 fps on M3/M4 Max, best with MetalFX)
profile.MEDIUM=Medium (M1/M2 Pro and Max, M3, M4)
profile.HIGH=High (M3/M4 Max: more torch lights and sharper shafts, about 60 fps)
profile.ULTRA=Ultra (M3/M4 Max: full-rate bounce light, best with MetalFX)
profile.comments=Presets per Mac. M3 and newer have ray-tracing hardware; on M1/M2 Low leaves out bounce light and light shafts, and MetalFX upscaling (mcmetal's MCMETAL_UPSCALE=1) is what gets a plain M1/M2 near 60 fps.
option.RAIN_PUDDLES=Rain Puddles
option.RAIN_PUDDLES.comment=Puddles on open ground when it rains, with ray-traced reflections.
option.PUDDLE_AMOUNT=Puddle Amount
option.RAIN_RIPPLES=Rain Ripples
option.RAIN_RIPPLES.comment=Raindrops make spreading rings on puddles.
option.WET_SHEEN=Wet Shine
option.WET_SHEEN.comment=Rain leaves a soft shine on walls, roofs and leaves the sky reaches.
option.GLASS_REFRACTION=Glass Refraction
option.GLASS_REFRACTION.comment=Glass bends and tints what is behind it, with reflections.
option.GLASS_REFRACTION_STRENGTH=Glass Distortion
option.GI_FILTER=GI Smoothing Taps
option.GI_FILTER.comment=How many neighbouring pixels smooth the bounce light. 9 is faster, 25 smoother.
option.LIGHT_CACHE=Light Cache (Multi-Bounce)
option.WORLD_CACHE=World Light Cache
option.WORLD_CACHE.comment=The bounce light is also remembered per block face in the world, so light keeps bouncing off things behind you and round corners, not just what is on screen. Needs Light Cache. Uses 16 MB.
option.LIGHT_CACHE.comment=Light bounces more than once: ray hits on screen reuse the bounce light already gathered there. Brighter, more even rooms, no extra rays.
option.DENOISER=GI Denoiser
option.DENOISER.comment=Two extra filter rounds that clean the grain out of the bounce light while keeping its light and shadow edges. Off: a little faster, grainier.
option.SHADOW_CHECKERBOARD=Half-Rate Shadow Rays
option.SHADOW_CHECKERBOARD.comment=Traces sun shadows for half the pixels each frame; the rest reuse the last result. Faster, very slightly slower to react.
option.SHADOW_RATE=Shadow Ray Rate
option.SHADOW_RATE.comment=With Half-Rate Shadow Rays on: trace sun shadows and light shafts for 1 in this many pixels each frame. 1 in 4 is faster; shadow edges may look a little grainier.
value.SHADOW_RATE.2=1 in 2
value.SHADOW_RATE.4=1 in 4
option.CAUSTICS=Caustics
option.CAUSTICS.comment=Moving rings of light on the bottom of sunlit water, and light shafts under water.
option.CAUSTICS_STRENGTH=Caustics Strength
option.LIGHT_SHAFTS=Light Shafts
option.LIGHT_SHAFTS.comment=Ray-traced god rays where sunlight comes through gaps.
option.LIGHT_SHAFTS_STRENGTH=Light Shaft Strength
option.LIGHT_SHAFTS_STEPS=Light Shaft Quality
option.COLORED_LIGHT=Coloured Block Light
option.COLORED_LIGHT.comment=Each light block lights the world in its own colour, with ray-traced shadows. Needs mcmetal.
option.COLORED_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Coloured Light Strength
option.LIGHT_SLOTS=Lights Per Pixel
option.LIGHT_SLOTS.comment=How many of the nearest light blocks each spot considers. More is slower.
option.SKY_GI_SATURATION=Sky Light Colour
option.SKY_GI_SATURATION.comment=How blue the light from the sky looks indoors. Lower is more neutral.
option.BLOCK_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Torch Light
option.EMISSIVE_STRENGTH=Glowing Blocks
option.BLOCK_LIGHT_R=Torch Red
option.BLOCK_LIGHT_G=Torch Green
option.BLOCK_LIGHT_B=Torch Blue
option.EXPOSURE=Brightness
option.SATURATION=Saturation
option.CONTRAST=Contrast
option.FOG_DENSITY=Haze
option.sunPathRotation=Sun Angle
option.WATER_SHADOWS=Shadows on Water
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Map Size
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Map Distance
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE=Eye Adaptation
option.GI_HALF_RES=Half-Res Bounce Light
screen.RAYS=Ray Tracing
option.RT_GI=Bounce Light (GI)
option.RT_AO=Ray-Traced AO
option.RT_GI_DISTANCE=Bounce Light Reach
option.RT_AO_RADIUS=AO Radius
option.RT_AO_FRAMES=AO Smoothing
option.SUN_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.COLORED_SHADOWS=Coloured Glass Shadows
option.GI_COARSE_RAYS=Fast Bounce Light
option.GI_COARSE_RAYS.comment=Bounce light sees leaves, grass and flowers more than 2 blocks away as solid, so its rays never stop to check their see-through holes. Faster in forests; the light is blurry anyway.
option.LIGHT_SHAFTS_RATE=Light Shaft Rate
option.LIGHT_SHAFTS_RATE.comment=Light shafts are traced for 1 in this many pixels each frame and averaged over frames. 4 is about twice as fast as 2 and looks the same, since shafts are soft.
option.RT_REFLECTIONS=Ray-Traced Reflections
option.RT_REFLECT_DISTANCE=Reflection Reach
option.WATER_REFLECT_HALF=Fast Water Reflections
option.WATER_REFLECT_HALF.comment=Traces the reflections on lakes and the sea at half resolution, for half the pixels each frame, and averages them over a few frames. Much faster, and almost the same picture.
option.WATER_DEPTH_COLOR=Water Depth Colour
option.WATER_DEPTH_COLOR.comment=Shallow water is clear, deep water turns blue-green and then dark, as light is absorbed on the way down.
option.WATER_DEPTH_COLOR_STRENGTH=Water Depth Strength
option.WATER_FOAM=Shore Foam
option.WATER_REFRACTION=Water Refraction
option.WATER_REFRACTION.comment=Traced refraction: the view bends where it enters water, so the bottom looks nearer and shifts with the waves. One extra ray per water pixel.
option.WATER_FOAM.comment=A thin moving line of foam where water meets the shore or anything standing in it.
option.WAVE_HEIGHT=Wave Height
option.WAVE_SPEED=Wave Speed
option.DEBUG_VIEW=Debug View
option.GI_RATE=Bounce Light Rate
option.GI_RATE.comment=Trace bounce light and ambient occlusion for 1 in this many pixels each frame; the rest reuse their average. 2 and 4 are much faster and may smear a little when things move.
value.GI_RATE.1=Every pixel
value.GI_RATE.2=1 in 2
value.GI_RATE.4=1 in 4
option.COLORED_LIGHT_GLASS=Coloured Glass Torchlight
option.COLORED_LIGHT_GLASS.comment=Light from torches and lanterns through stained glass takes the glass's colour.
option.SHARP_LIGHT_SHADOWS=Sharp Light Shadows
option.SHARP_LIGHT_SHADOWS.comment=Torches and lamps cast crisp, hard-edged shadows. Off gives soft shadows.
option.STYLE=Style
option.STYLE.comment=The look of the world: its sky, light, mist and glow. Natural: true to life. Cottage: golden afternoons, peach sunsets, morning mist, long light shafts. Witchy: violet dusks, bright purple moonlit nights with aurora, ember torches, thick valley mist. Storybook: cartoon sky, banded toon light and ink outlines. Fairytale: pink and turquoise skies, rose shade, sparkling glow.
value.STYLE.0=Natural
value.STYLE.1=Cottage
value.STYLE.2=Witchy
value.STYLE.3=Storybook
value.STYLE.4=Fairytale
option.LABPBR_NORMAL_STRENGTH=PBR Depth
option.LABPBR_NORMAL_STRENGTH.comment=How deep the bumps, cracks and mortar lines of a LabPBR resource pack look.
option.ROUGH_REFLECTIONS_STRENGTH=PBR Sheen
option.ROUGH_REFLECTIONS_STRENGTH.comment=The soft sheen of rough and satin blocks in a LabPBR pack (stone, wood, brick): a blurred reflection of the sky and the light around them.
option.SEASONS=Seasons
option.SEASONS.comment=Light, sky, clouds and mist follow the year: fresh spring mornings with mist, warm summer sun, golden autumn light with thicker mist, pale winter sun with grey skies and frost. Follows Serene Seasons' calendar from the world's clock; your chosen Style stays on top.
option.SEASON_LENGTH=Days per Sub-season
option.SEASON_LENGTH.comment=Match Serene Seasons' sub_season_duration (8 by default). A season is three sub-seasons.
option.SEASON_OFFSET=Season Offset (days)
option.SEASON_OFFSET.comment=Moves the shader's calendar on by this many days, if it is out of step with the mod (for example after /season set).
option.VOLUMETRIC_MIST=Morning Mist
option.VOLUMETRIC_MIST.comment=Mist near the ground at sunrise and in rain, lit up by the sun's beams. Needs Light Shafts.
option.MIST_AMOUNT=Mist Amount
option.SUBSURFACE=Leaf Glow
option.SUBSURFACE.comment=Leaves and grass let sunlight through: with the sun behind them they glow a deeper green.
option.SUBSURFACE_STRENGTH=Leaf Glow Strength
option.SUBSURFACE_STRENGTH.comment=How much sunlight shines through leaves and grass.
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH=Lightning Flashes
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH.comment=Lightning bolts light up the land and the sky in a flickering blue-white flash.
option.LIGHTNING_STRENGTH=Lightning Brightness
option.LIGHTNING_STRENGTH.comment=How bright a lightning flash is.
option.CIRRUS=High Wispy Clouds
option.CIRRUS.comment=Thin streaks of ice cloud far above the main clouds.
option.DAILY_WEATHER=Daily Skies
option.DAILY_WEATHER.comment=Each day has its own sky: some clear, some cloudy. The same for everyone in the world.
option.WAVING_PLANTS=Waving Plants
option.WAVING_PLANTS.comment=Grass, flowers, crops and leaves sway gently in the wind, more in rain.
option.WAVING_AMOUNT=Waving Amount
option.WAVING_AMOUNT.comment=How far plants and leaves sway.
option.WAVING_SPEED=Waving Speed
option.WAVING_SPEED.comment=How fast plants and leaves sway.
option.AUTO_PBR=Automatic Materials
option.AUTO_PBR.comment=Blocks without PBR maps still look their part: ores glint, metal blocks shine, gems and polished stone are glossy. Works on modded blocks too.
option.AUTO_PBR_STRENGTH=Automatic Material Shine
option.AUTO_PBR_STRENGTH.comment=How glossy the automatic materials are.
option.LAMP_FOG=Lamp-Lit Fog
option.LAMP_FOG.comment=Torches, lanterns and glowing blocks light up the air round them: a soft glow in fog, rain and dusty rooms.
option.LAMP_FOG_STRENGTH=Lamp Fog Strength
option.LAMP_FOG_STRENGTH.comment=How much the air glows round lamps.
option.SHARPEN=Sharpen
option.SHARPEN.comment=A light sharpen after anti-aliasing, so textures stay crisp.
option.SHARPEN_STRENGTH=Sharpen Strength
option.SHARPEN_STRENGTH.comment=How much the picture is sharpened.
option.TONEMAP=Tone Curve
option.TONEMAP.comment=How bright light is fitted to the screen. ACES is punchy; Soft Filmic has gentler highlights and truer bright colours.
value.TONEMAP.0=ACES Filmic
value.TONEMAP.1=Soft Filmic
option.PURKINJE=Night Vision Tint
option.PURKINJE.comment=In very dim light colours fade and lean blue, the way eyes see at night.
option.PURKINJE_STRENGTH=Night Vision Tint Strength
option.STARS=Stars
option.STARS.comment=Our own steady night sky: stars of many sizes and colours that turn through the night.
option.MILKY_WAY=Milky Way
option.MILKY_WAY.comment=The faint band of the Milky Way, with dark dust lanes.
option.STARS_BRIGHTNESS=Star Brightness
option.RT_NOISE=Ray Noise
option.RT_NOISE.comment=How rays pick their random directions. Decorrelated noise leaves fewer patterns for the denoiser.
value.RT_NOISE.0=Classic
value.RT_NOISE.1=Decorrelated
option.RAINBOW=Rainbows
option.RAINBOW.comment=A rainbow opposite the sun as the rain clears.
option.RAINBOW_STRENGTH=Rainbow Strength
option.LIGHT_POLLUTION=Lamp Glow In The Sky
option.LIGHT_POLLUTION.comment=At night, a lit base makes a warm glow low in the sky.
option.LIGHT_POLLUTION_STRENGTH=Lamp Glow Strength
option.END_BEAMS=End Sky Beams
option.END_BEAMS.comment=In the End, violet beams rise out of the void under faint stars.
option.END_BEAMS_STRENGTH=End Beams Strength
option.PHOTO_MODE=Photo Mode
option.PHOTO_MODE.comment=While you stand still, rays keep averaging much longer for clean screenshots. Lights settle more slowly while still.
option.PHOTO_FRAMES=Photo Mode Frames
option.UNIFIED_TARGETS=One Pass For See-Through
option.UNIFIED_TARGETS.comment=Particles, rain and other see-through things share the same buffers as water so they draw in one pass (faster on Metal).
option.PARALLAX=Parallax Depth
option.PARALLAX.comment=Resource packs with height maps (Vanilla RTX) give bricks and cobbles real depth up close.
option.PARALLAX_DEPTH=Parallax Depth Amount
option.PARALLAX_STEPS=Parallax Quality
option.GI_ADAPTIVE=Adaptive Ray Rate
option.GI_ADAPTIVE.comment=Newly seen spots trace bounce light every frame, settled ones less often. Faster; lights change a little more slowly.
option.GI_SHORT_RAYS=Short Bounce Rays
option.GI_SHORT_RAYS.comment=Faster: bounce-light rays stop after a few blocks and use the sky light Minecraft gives beyond that.
option.GI_SHORT_DISTANCE=Short Ray Length
option.DENOISE_PASSES=Denoiser Passes
option.DENOISE_PASSES.comment=Rounds of the bounce-light denoiser. One does the same reach in a single wider pass, which is one render pass fewer.
option.HALF_PRECISION=Half Precision
option.HALF_PRECISION.comment=The denoiser's maths in 16-bit numbers, Apple's advice for faster shaders. Only on mcmetal from 10-26 or newer; elsewhere it does nothing.
option.METALFX_DENOISE=MetalFX Denoiser
option.METALFX_DENOISE.comment=Apple's denoiser cleans the whole lit picture. Needs mcmetal with MCMETAL_DENOISE=1, an M3 or newer and macOS 26. Replaces the pack's own denoiser.
option.SHAFT_BUDGET=Light Shaft Budget
option.SHAFT_BUDGET.comment=Fewer light-shaft rays where you look at something close (rooms, walls): one step every few blocks instead of the full count.
option.SHAFT_STEP_LENGTH=Shaft Step Length
option.SHAFT_STEP_LENGTH.comment=With Light Shaft Budget: blocks of air per light-shaft step. Longer is faster, shorter is smoother.
option.HELD_LIGHT_SHADOWS=Hand Light Shadows
option.HELD_LIGHT_SHADOWS.comment=The torch or lantern in your hand casts shadows. One ray for each pixel it lights while you hold it.
option.END_PORTAL_STARS=End Portal Stars
option.END_PORTAL_STARS.comment=A deep starfield inside End portals and gateways, with layers that slide past each other as you move.
option.END_PORTAL_BRIGHTNESS=End Portal Brightness
option.AURORA=Northern Lights
option.AURORA.comment=Northern lights at a real height over the world, in every look. They stay put as you walk and you can fly through them. Replaces Witchy's painted aurora.
option.AURORA_HEIGHT=Northern Lights Height
option.AURORA_SCALE=Northern Lights Size
option.AURORA_SPEED=Northern Lights Speed
option.AURORA_BRIGHTNESS=Northern Lights Brightness
option.PIXEL_SHADOWS=Pixel Shadows
option.PIXEL_SHADOWS.comment=Sun shadows snap to the blocks' own pixels, with stepped edges like Minecraft's textures. Suits the Storybook and Fairytale looks.
option.GLOSSY_RT=Traced Satin Sheen
option.GLOSSY_RT.comment=Satin PBR blocks (polished stone, wood, brick) close to you trace one short ray for their soft reflection, so it shows the torch or wall really there instead of a guess. Costs a ray per satin pixel.
option.GLOSSY_RT_DISTANCE=Traced Sheen Distance
option.LIGHT_RESTIR=Many-Light Sampling (ReSTIR)
option.LIGHT_RESTIR.comment=Each pixel remembers which nearby light it picked last frame and how well that worked, so in a room full of candles it settles on the lights it can actually see. Less flicker and faster settling. Uses 32 MB.
option.REFLECTION_DENOISE=Reflection Denoiser
option.REFLECTION_DENOISE.comment=Glossy traced reflections are averaged over frames (rougher surfaces for longer), so they look smooth instead of grainy. Mirrors are left sharp. Uses 64 MB.
